                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p69-q2-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply the sine rule in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\triangle ABD",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", using ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "BD=1-y",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Since $\\angle BAC=45^\\circ$ and $AD$ bisects this angle, $\\angle BAD=22.5^\\circ$. Also, $BD=BC-CD=1-y$ and $\\angle ABD=45^\\circ$.\n\nThe sine rule in $\\triangle ABD$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\sin\\angle BAD}{BD}&=\\frac{\\sin\\angle ABD}{AD}\\\\\n\\frac{\\sin22.5^\\circ}{1-y}&=\\frac{\\sin45^\\circ}{x}\\\\\n\\frac{\\sin22.5^\\circ}{1-y}&=\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt2}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
