        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p69-q2-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan22.5^\\circ=\\sqrt2-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p69-q2-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan22.5^\\circ=y",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin22.5^\\circ=\\frac{y}{x}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " in part (a), then rationalise.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In $\\triangle CAD$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\tan22.5^\\circ&=\\frac{CD}{AC}=y,\\\\\n\\sin22.5^\\circ&=\\frac{CD}{AD}=\\frac{y}{x}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into part (a). Since $x>0$ and $0<y<1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{y}{x(1-y)}&=\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt2}\\\\\n\\sqrt2\\,y&=1-y\\\\\n(\\sqrt2+1)y&=1\\\\\ny&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2+1}\\\\\ny&=\\sqrt2-1\\\\\n\\tan22.5^\\circ&=\\sqrt2-1.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      }
    ]
